# Automatic HTTPS for the Metis demo. Caddy fetches and renews a Let's Encrypt
# certificate for METIS_DEMO_HOST, then reverse-proxies everything (including the
# run-status WebSocket, which Caddy upgrades transparently) to the Metis app.
{$METIS_DEMO_HOST} {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy metis:3000
}

# A www -> apex redirect used to live here. It was not harmless: Caddy tries to
# obtain a certificate for every site block, and www.<host> has no DNS record on
# a real domain (app.metisflow.io is already a subdomain, and sslip.io hosts have
# no www either). Every attempt failed the ACME challenge with NXDOMAIN, retried
# for the full 30-day window, and eventually fell back to the staging CA. If a
# deployment genuinely serves www, add the block back with the DNS record first.
